## 1. Component graph

The probe is a **procedure**, not code: hand-extraction performed by an agent under a
fixed rubric. The components below are procedural stages with typed hand-offs, specified
to the same standard as software components so the run is reproducible by a second
operator (§5.1 rule 3's reproducibility ethos applied to the probe itself).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    SEL["C1 Goal Selector<br/>picks 3 sealed goals"]
    SRC["C2 Source Resolver<br/>review artifact + 1 citation hop"]
    CEN["C3 Field Census<br/>frozen §3.2 matrix — 12 types, 3 bands"]
    EXT["C4 Type Extractors ×11<br/>one per scored §4.3 node type"]
    LED["C5 Cell Ledger<br/>append-only ProbeCell records"]
    SCO["C6 Scorer<br/>content_score + anchor + recoverable_elsewhere"]
    AGG["C7 Aggregator<br/>band ratios, type presence, veto set"]
    ADJ["C8 Adjudicator<br/>VETO check then ratio check"]
    EMI["C9 Report Emitter<br/>frontmatter + per-goal sections"]

    SEL -->|"GoalRef[3]"| SRC
    SRC -->|"SourceSet per goal"| EXT
    CEN -->|"ScorableCell[] (denominator)"| EXT
    CEN -->|"veto field set"| ADJ
    EXT -->|"raw finding per cell"| SCO
    SCO -->|"ProbeCell"| LED
    LED -->|"all cells"| AGG
    AGG -->|"ProbeAggregate"| ADJ
    ADJ -->|"Verdict + carries"| EMI
    LED -->|"per-goal cells"| EMI
    AGG -->|"ratios"| EMI
    EMI -->|"reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md"| OUT["accept assertions (§10)"]
```

**Placement rationale.** The census (C3) is separated from the extractors (C4) so the
**denominator is fixed before any source is read**. If the extractor defined its own field
list per goal, the loss ratio would be self-selecting — an extractor that only looks for
what it finds always reports zero loss. Freezing C3 in this document, ahead of C2, is what
makes the probe a falsification test rather than a demonstration. This is the probe-level
analogue of SAEOS-1 §4.1's design rule (derive backwards from a ratified consumer, not
forwards from what happens to be available).

**No orphan:** every component has at least one inbound and one outbound edge except C1
(entry) and C9 (exit); C3 is a pure source consumed by C4 and C8.

