## 9. Hand-off to the executing stage

**Capability required:** read `reviews/tasks/`, write `reviews/spikes/`. This design
session holds neither (§0).

**Output path:** `reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`.

**Required structure** (exact line forms; the accept assertions are anchored regexes):

| Element | Exact form | Constraint |
|---|---|---|
| Frontmatter open | `---` | Line 1. |
| Verdict | `verdict: GO` **or** `verdict: NO-GO` | Exactly one such line; nothing before or after on the line. |
| Loss ratio | `loss_ratio: 0.NN` | 2 decimals, half-up. Band A, one-hop SourceSet. See A8′ for the `1.00` case. |
| Supporting keys | `loss_ratio_review_only`, `band_b_loss`, `anchor_loss_ratio`, `basis`, `probed_goals`, `design_ref` | `design_ref` cites this file. |
| Frontmatter close | `---` | |
| Per-goal section | a level-2 heading of the form `## goal: ` followed by the goal id | **Exactly one per probed goal, ≥ 3 total.** |

**Body per goal section:** the `SourceSet` used (with hop-1 paths), weight class and trace
(A5), `instances_found` per node type, the full `ProbeCell` table
(`type · field · band · score · anchor · hop · recoverable_elsewhere · note`), and the
goal's `band_a_loss`.

**Then, once:** the aggregate tables (`type_presence`, `veto_failures`, all ratios), the
adjudication trace through §6.2, and the carries — minimally A3, A5, A6/anchor, plus the
A2 divergence finding if triggered.

> **Format trap — read this before drafting.** The accept check is
> `rg -c '^## goal: '`, which counts **every** line starting with that string, including
> lines inside fenced code blocks. Do **not** paste a section template containing a literal
> `## goal:` heading into the report; it will inflate the count and decouple it from the
> number of goals actually probed. Describe the heading inline (as this table does) or in a
> `|`-prefixed table row. Also note `rg -c` exits non-zero and prints nothing when there
> are no matches, which makes `test $(rg -c …) -ge 3` a shell error rather than a clean
> failure — one more reason the headings must be real.

**Execution order:** §2.1 → §2.2 → §5 (per cell) → §4.1 → §6.2 → emit. Do not compute any
ratio before the census is fully enumerated; a partial denominator produces a wrong number
that looks right.

